<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Ahmadili dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1122 CE – 1225 CE (approx.) · capital Maragheh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A line of Turkish atabegs that ruled Maragheh in Azerbaijan in the 12th century, rivals of the Eldiguzids for power in north-western Iran.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadil-ibn-ibrahim">Ahmadil ibn Ibrahim</a>, a Kurdish emir of the Rawwadid family, held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maragha">Maragheh</a> under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> until he was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari Ismailis</a> in 1116. His Turkish mamluk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-sunqur-ahmadili">Aq Sunqur Ahmadili</a> succeeded him around 1122 and founded a dynasty named after his former master.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Ahmadilis governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maragha">Maragheh</a> and its region as atabegs, nominally guardians of Seljuk princes, and took part in the struggles of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seljuk-sultanate-of-iraq">Seljuk Sultanate of Iraq</a>. Aq Sunqur and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-sunqur-ii">Aq Sunqur II</a> backed rival sultans against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eldiguzids">Eldiguzids</a>. Maragheh flourished as a regional city with fine brick tomb towers, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonbad-e-sorkh">Gonbad-e Sorkh</a> of 1147.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maragha">Maragheh</a> in 1221, and around 1225 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshah</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalal-al-din-mangburni">Jalal al-Din Mangburni</a> took the city from the last representative of the dynasty, a woman ruler.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1122 CE – 1225 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.03%;width:2.05%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1122 CE – 1225 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Maragheh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aq Sunqur I, Aq Sunqur II, Ala al-Din Korpe Arslan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ahmadilis, Atabegs of Maragheh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1174&amp;focus=ahmadili-dynasty" aria-label="Ahmadili dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5836 832 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ahmadili dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6156 1088L6231 1174M6156 1088L6480 1127"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6231 1174h0M6480 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6156 1088h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6156 1088h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Maragheh. <a href="/atlas?year=1174&amp;focus=ahmadili-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

